1) unpack OP4STARS_1.3.tar.gz in your mesa work directory.
in its default mode, MESA users do not need to compile or run the codes in this directory.


2) set 2 environment variables similar to the following:

setenv MESA_OP_MONO_DATA_PATH /Users/bpaxton/OP4STARS_1.3/mono
setenv MESA_OP_MONO_DATA_CACHE_FILENAME /Users/bpaxton/OP4STARS_1.3/mono/op_mono_cache.bin


3) see the $MESA_DIR/star/test_suite/radiative_levitation test case
for an example of how to use the OP_MONO opacities.

you will know the OP_MONO opacities are nominally working when you see this output from MESA:

loading OP mono data...
done loading OP mono data
write /Users/fxt/mesa_work/OP4STARS_1.3/mono/op_mono_cache.bin
